# Home Assistant integration discipline

Apply when editing `custom_components/maxpreps/**` or HA integration tests (`tests/test_{config,coordinator,sensor,init}*`).

- MaxPreps HTML/JSON parsing stays in `parsing/` and the existing client; HA modules consume normalized models only
- All network I/O goes through the injectable async transport and coordinator; entities must not fetch
- Automated tests must not perform live MaxPreps HTTP
- Do not invent `contestState` mappings, timezone offsets, or sport→calendar tables
- Use the evidence-based supported-format allowlist from the approved Phase 3 plan — not a denylist of “likely” sports
- One subscribed-sport fetch/parse failure must not collapse the entire config entry to unavailable
- Do not require YAML for user configuration
- Do not start a custom Lovelace card in Phase 3
- Public-repo hygiene still applies ([public-repo-hygiene.mdc](public-repo-hygiene.mdc))
- Prefer HA helpers (`DataUpdateCoordinator`, `CoordinatorEntity`, `async_get_clientsession`, `DeviceInfo`, `OptionsFlowWithReload`) over bespoke substitutes
